trading-ui-help-title = Trading Help
trading-ui-help-buying-title = Buying
trading-ui-help-buying-text = Select an item and press the button with the yellow price. Funds are deducted from the balance, and the purchased item is given to you.
trading-ui-help-selling-title = Selling
trading-ui-help-selling-text = The button with the red price sells a suitable item from your active hand to the best available order. You can only sell items to other merchants; guilds will not accept your item.
trading-ui-help-listing-title = Listing a lot
trading-ui-help-listing-text = Hold an item in your active hand, enter a price in the bottom panel, and press “List lot”. The item remains in the trading pit until the lot is purchased or cancelled. After the lot is purchased, collect the revenue in offer management.
trading-ui-help-common-order-title = Ordering a common item
trading-ui-help-common-order-text = Open the “Common” section, select an item, enter the order price on the right, and press “Order”. The specified amount is reserved until the order is fulfilled or cancelled.
trading-ui-help-sample-order-title = Ordering from a sample
trading-ui-help-sample-order-text = Hold the desired item in your active hand, enter a price in the bottom panel, and press “Create order from sample”. The sample identifies the requested item and is not consumed when the order is created, but the money required for the order is reserved until the order is fulfilled or cancelled.
trading-ui-help-management-title = Management
trading-ui-help-management-text = The offer management section lets you cancel your lots and orders, collect revenue from sold lots, and collect items delivered after a successful order. The archive stores records of your completed trades.

